Emulate /dev/zero and /dev/urandom only for O_SPECIAL opens.
mingw_open called update_special_fd after every open of /dev/zero or
/dev/urandom, including a plain write-only open, which goes to the null
device. That replaced the descriptor of an earlier O_SPECIAL open, and
closing the null device one then cleared it, so the earlier descriptor
read from the null device instead. "shred -z /dev/zero FILE" thus wrote
no zeros to FILE, and "shred /dev/urandom FILE" no random data, yet
both exited with status 0. Record the descriptor only for O_SPECIAL
opens, which are the ones the emulation is for.

---
 win32/mingw.c |    3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/win32/mingw.c
+++ b/win32/mingw.c
@@ -270,7 +270,8 @@
 
 	fd = open(filename, oflags&~O_SPECIAL, pmode);
 	if (fd >= 0) {
-		update_special_fd(dev, fd);
+		if (special)
+			update_special_fd(dev, fd);
 	}
 	else if ((oflags & O_ACCMODE) != O_RDONLY && errno == EACCES) {
 		if (mingw_is_directory(filename))
